          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematics"} mathematics
            (also “mathematical structure”) is often taken to be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            equipped with some choice of elements, with some operations and some relations. Such as for instance the “structure of a
            = succeed "\u201D." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+theory"} model theory
            this concept of mathematical structure is formalized by way of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+logic"} formal logic
          %p
            Notice however that by far not every concept studied in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematics"} mathematics
            fits as an example of a mathematical structure in the sense of classical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first-order+theory"} first order
            model theory, described
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Definition"} below
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            fails to be a structure in the sense of classical model theory (see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#MathSEDisc"} here
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            there is a more flexible concept of
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
          %h2#Definition Definition
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first-order+language"} first-order language
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variable"} variable symbols
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+symbols"} function symbols
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation"} relation
            symbols including
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantifiers"} quantifiers
            %strong structure
            for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            = succeed "-structure\u201D," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            with an
            %strong interpretation
            for symbols:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R\in L
                is an
                = succeed "-ary" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation"} relation
                symbol, then its interpretation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi R
                        %mi M
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msup
                        %mi M
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R^M\subset M^n
            %li
              %p
                if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\in L
                is an
                = succeed "-ary" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
                symbol, then
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mi M
                      %mo :
                      %msup
                        %mi M
                        %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^M:M^n\to M
                is a function
            %li
              %p
                if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c\in L
                is a constant symbol, then
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi c
                        %mi M
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c^M\in M
          %p
            The underlying set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            of the structure is referred to as (universal)
            %strong domain
            of the structure (or the universe of the structure).
          %p
            Interpretation for an
            = succeed "-structure" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi\in L
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/true"} true
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi^M
            is true. Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theory"} theory
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo ,
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L,T)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            together with a given set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            of sentences in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axioms"}> axioms
            ), the interpretation in a structure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            makes those sentences true or false; if all the sentences in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            are true in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            we say that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model"} model
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo ,
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L,T)
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+theory"} model theory
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            is the same as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model"} model
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theory"} theory
            with an empty set of axioms. Conversely, a
            %em model
            of a theory is a
            %em structure
            of its underlying language that satisfies the axioms demanded by that theory.
          %p There is a generalization of structure for languages/theories with multiple domains or sorts, called multi-sorted languages/theories.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#elementary_classes_of_structures Elementary classes of structures
          %p
            A class
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            of structures of a given signature is an
            %strong elementary class
            if there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first-order+theory"} first-order theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            consists precisely of all models of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
          %p
            There is a vast generalizations for higher-order theories (and more), see at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abstract+elementary+class"} abstract elementary class
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+abstract+elementary+class"} metric abstract elementary class
          %h3#categories_of_structures Categories of structures
          %p
            Every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+category"} algebraic category
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            preserves
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimits"} filtered colimits
            is the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/models"} models
            for some
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first-order+theory"} first-order theory
          %p
            A detailed discussion of characterizations of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
            of structures in the sense of model theory is in (
            %a{:href => "#BekeRosciky11"}> Beke-Rosciky 11
            ).
          %h3#CategoricalInterpretation Interpretation in categorical logic
          %p
            Every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first-order+language"} first-order language
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            gives rise to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first-order+hyperdoctrine"} first-order hyperdoctrine
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equality"} equality
            freely generated from
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(L)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi L
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{T(L)}
            consists of sorts (which are products of basic sorts) and functional terms between sorts; the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/predicates"} predicates
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+classes"} equivalence classes
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relations"} relations
            definable in the language. The construction of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(L)
            depends to some extent on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/logic"} logic
            we wish to impose; for example, we could take the free
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+hyperdoctrine"} Boolean hyperdoctrine
            generated from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            if we work in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+logic"} classical logic
          %p
            There is also a “tautological” first order hyperdoctrine whose base category is
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi Bool
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \colon Set^{op} \to Bool
          %p
            and then an interpretation of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Taut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(L) \to Taut(Set)
          %p
            This observation opens the door to a widened interpretation of “interpretation” in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+logic"} categorical logic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            to any other
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sub
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi Heyt
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub \colon E^{op} \to Heyt
            (taking an object of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            to its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+algebra"} Heyting algebra
            of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobjects"} subobjects
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+theory"} model theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first-order+theory"} first-order theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interpretation"} interpretation
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram+of+a+first-order+structure"} diagram of a first-order structure
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exceptional+structure"} exceptional structure
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/amalgamation+property"} amalgamation property
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"}> structure
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+structure"} higher structure
          %h2#references References
          %p Standard textbook accounts include
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wilfrid+Hodges"}> Wilfrid Hodges
                , section 1 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A shorter model theory
            %li
              %p
                Chen Chung Chang,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H.+Jerome+Keisler"} H. Jerome Keisler
                = succeed "." do
                  %em Model Theory. Studies in Logic and the Foundations of Mathematics
          %p
            Characterizations of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
            of model-theoretic structures and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
            between them (certain accessible categories) is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#BekeRosciky11
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tibor+Beke"}> Tibor Beke
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ji%C5%99%C3%AD+Rosick%C3%BD"} Jiří Rosický
              = succeed "," do
                %em Abstract elementary classes and accessible categories
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.muni.cz/~rosicky/papers/elem7.pdf"} pdf
          %p Online discussion includes
          %ul
            %li#MathSEDisc
              Math.SE
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://math.stackexchange.com/questions/97856/topological-spaces-as-model-theoretic-structures-definitions"} Topological spaces as model-theoretic structures — definitions?
          .property
            category:
            %a.category_link{:href => "/nlab/all_pages/model+theory"} model theory
